<tbody>
<tr><td>Education and health services</td><td><strong class="ex-n">6100</strong>（總數最多）</td><td><strong class="ex-n">4</strong>（第 2）</td></tr>
<tr><td>Manufacturing</td><td><strong class="ex-n">4400</strong>（總數第 2）</td><td>—</td></tr>
<tr><td>Natural resources and mining</td><td><strong class="ex-n">1000</strong></td><td><strong class="ex-n">5.5</strong>（發生率最高）</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p class="ex-cite">p.439；Fig. 27-2，p.441。</p>
<aside class="ex-trap"><strong>易錯</strong>病例「總數」最多是 education and health services，「發生率」最高是 natural resources and mining。</aside>
<ul>
<li>OSD 總數與需請假病例近十年下降（預防與早期處置進步）。<span class="ex-ref">p.439</span></li>
<li>2014 年 skin infections 造成請假時間最長（median <strong class="ex-n">6 days</strong>）；wounds and bruises 的請假發生率最高（<strong class="ex-n">9.1</strong> per 10,000）。</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section class="ex-note" id="ocd">
<h2>3. Occupational Contact Dermatitis: ICD vs ACD（職業性接觸性皮膚炎）</h2>
<ul>
<li>ICD：對化學、物理或機械刺激的 <strong>nonimmunologic</strong> 反應，經 direct cytotoxic effect 造成發炎；任何人都可能發生，<strong>atopic dermatitis、xerosis、淺膚色</strong>等屏障受損者風險較高。<span class="ex-ref">p.439</span></li>
<li><mark data-q="114-15">ACD：<strong>type IV、delayed hypersensitivity</strong>，cell-mediated，需要先致敏</mark>；過敏原通常是作為 hapten 的 low-molecular-weight chemical，只有少數人會發生。</li>
<li>已知 <strong class="ex-n">&gt;57,000</strong> 種化學物可造成刺激（ICD），真正的皮膚過敏原只有約 <strong class="ex-n">3700</strong> 種。</li>
<li><mark data-q="105-47,107-48">OCD 絕大部分發生在手部（<strong class="ex-n">80%</strong>）</mark>。<span class="ex-ref">p.439</span></li>
</ul>
<aside class="ex-trap"><strong>易錯</strong><mark data-q="114-15">ICD 是 nonimmunologic 反應；immunologic contact urticaria（ICU）是 allergen-specific IgE 介導的 type I hypersensitivity</mark>。</aside>
<table class="ex-table">
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Feature</th><th scope="col">Irritant（ICD）</th><th scope="col">Allergic（ACD）</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Onset</td><td>強刺激物數分鐘內；弱刺激物可達數天至數週</td><td>已致敏者 <strong class="ex-n">24–96 h</strong></td></tr>
<tr><td>Resolution</td><td>離開暴露 <strong class="ex-n">3–6 weeks</strong> 後改善</td><td>暴露後數天內可改善；部分持續</td></tr>
<tr><td>Histology</td><td>Spongiotic dermatitis</td><td>Spongiotic dermatitis</td></tr>
<tr><td>Mechanism</td><td>Nonimmune、不需致敏；epidermal barrier disruption、epidermal cellular damage、keratinocytes 釋放 pro-inflammatory mediators</td><td>Immune-mediated、需致敏；antigen-activated primed T cells；sensitization phase 通常 <strong class="ex-n">10–14 d</strong></td></tr>
<tr><td>Agent</td><td>Concentration dependent</td><td>Not concentration dependent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Atopy</td><td>Predisposition（易感）</td><td>Variable</td></tr>
<tr><td>Diagnosis</td><td>Clinical</td><td>Patch testing</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
